  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 312 PM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nConvection activity has continued to taper off the last few hours as \nthe atmosphere continues to stabilize. The aforementioned boundary \nwill continue to track out of the region with drier air filtering in \nit's wake. Mid-level high pressure will build over the next couple \nof days taking over by midweek. Expect this to promote warm and \nmostly rain free conditions outside of likely seabreeze convection. \nWith the ridge building, so will those ugly feels like temps. We \nwill see heat indices up to 115 as early as Tuesday with dew points \naround the mid to upper 70s present. This translates to Moderate\nto Major heat stress conditions. We strongly encourage the \npractice of heat safety in these conditions. Take frequent breaks \nand remember to stay hydrated, check those backseats, and avoid \nlong exposure in these temperatures. For more information be sure \nto check out weather.gov/heatsafety.",
